---

<Layout
  title="CMI Qualifications for NHS Managers | Levels, Units and Evidence"
  description="How NHS and health and care managers can choose a CMI level, which units suit their work, and how to use CQC and WRES evidence in assignments."
  canonical={siteUrl + '/guides/nhs-management-cmi-qualifications/'}
  pageSchema={[articleSchema, faqSchema]}
>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">NHS and Health and Care Managers &bull; CQC &bull; WRES &bull; NHS People Plan</p>
      <h1>CMI Qualifications for NHS Managers | Levels, Units and Evidence</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        How an NHS or health and care manager can choose a CMI level, which units suit the work, and where CQC
        and WRES evidence can support a CMI assignment. Written for managers studying CMI Level 5 or Level 7
        alongside a full-time role.
      </p>
      <a href={whatsappUrl} class="btn btn-whatsapp btn-lg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Get NHS CMI Assignment Help
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <img
    class="page-header-img"
    src="/images/headers/nhs-management-cmi-qualifications.webp"
    alt="CMI qualifications for NHS managers"
    width="1376"
    height="688"
    loading="eager"
    decoding="async"
  />

  <TableOfContents />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="why-nhs-managers-study-cmi">Why NHS Managers Study CMI Qualifications</h2>
      <p>
        CMI qualifications are professional management and leadership qualifications used by managers in every
        sector, including the NHS. They are built from units with defined assessment criteria, so they give a
        structured way to develop and evidence your management practice.
      </p>
      <p>Common reasons NHS managers give for studying CMI:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Structured development</strong>: the units cover leading teams, change, risk, finance, equality and more, with criteria you can map to your own role.</li>
        <li><strong>A route to Chartered Manager</strong>: CMI says all successful Level 5 learners are eligible for Foundation Chartered Manager (fCMgr), and Diploma and Extended Diploma learners at Levels 5 and 7 may be eligible for Chartered Manager (CMgr) with at least three years of management and leadership experience.</li>
        <li><strong>Flexible study</strong>: assessment is coursework set by your centre against CMI's criteria, with written work forming the majority of the evidence, so it can be done alongside a job.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        For how CMI membership grades work, see <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/cmi-membership-levels-acmi-mcmi-fcmi/">CMI membership grades explained</a>.
        Whether a given qualification is listed in a job's person specification is for the employer, so check the specification for the role you want.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="cmi-by-nhs-band">Choosing a CMI Level for Your Role</h2>
      <p>
        NHS Agenda for Change bands are not a CMI concept, and CMI does not map its levels to them. Choose by the scope of
        your role, using the roles CMI names for each level.
      </p>
      <div class="band-table">
        <div class="band-row">
          <div class="band-name">CMI Level 3</div>
          <div class="band-detail">
            <span class="band-roles">Units 301 to 321: first-line and team-level management</span>
            <span>&rarr; <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-3-assignment-help/">CMI Level 3 assignment help</a></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="band-row band-row--highlight">
          <div class="band-name">CMI Level 5</div>
          <div class="band-detail">
            <span class="band-roles">Operations, Divisional, Departmental, Regional and Specialist Managers, typically accountable to a senior manager</span>
            <span>&rarr; <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-5-assignment-help/">CMI Level 5 assignment help</a>: units 501 to 526</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="band-row">
          <div class="band-name">CMI Level 6</div>
          <div class="band-detail">
            <span class="band-roles">Professional Management and Leadership Practice, between Levels 5 and 7</span>
            <span>&rarr; <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-6-assignment-help/">CMI Level 6 assignment help</a>: units 601 to 614</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="band-row band-row--highlight">
          <div class="band-name">CMI Level 7</div>
          <div class="band-detail">
            <span class="band-roles">Senior Manager, Regional Manager, Specialist Manager, Director and CEO</span>
            <span>&rarr; <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-7-assignment-help/">CMI Level 7 assignment help</a>: units 701 to 716</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="band-note">
        Your centre decides whether you have the capability for a level, and your employer's learning and development
        plan usually decides which programme is offered.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="cmi-level-5-for-band-7">CMI Level 5 for Team and Service Managers</h2>
      <p>
        CMI describes the primary role at Level 5 as leading and managing individuals and teams to deliver aims and
        objectives in line with organisational strategy. That fits ward managers, clinical managers, service managers
        and team leaders, who already have deep operational and clinical expertise.
      </p>
      <p>
        The challenge for many health and care managers is not the knowledge. It is turning that expertise into
        written evidence for each assessment criterion. The criteria use verbs such as Analyse, Examine and Evaluate,
        and your assignment needs to do what the verb asks, using your own team and service as the case. Our
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/cmi-command-verbs-explained/">command verbs guide</a> explains each verb.
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-5-assignment-help/">CMI Level 5 assignment help</a>
        works from your unit criteria and your brief.
      </p>
      <p>Level 5 units carry a guideline of 3,000 to 5,000 words, with a 10% allowance above or below. Your brief sets the figure for your unit.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="cmi-level-7-for-band-8">CMI Level 7 for Senior Health and Care Leaders</h2>
      <p>
        CMI Level 7, Strategic Management and Leadership Practice, is designed for practising or aspiring senior
        managers and leaders, with roles such as Senior Manager, Director and CEO. Its units are about strategy,
        organisational design, risk, finance, change and leading people at organisation-wide scope. Of the 80
        criteria, 37 begin with Critically, and many end with a proposal or strategy, so the work needs to judge the
        evidence and then recommend.
      </p>
      <p>
        Senior health and care leaders work within the governance and accountability structures of trusts and Integrated
        Care Systems, which gives plenty of material for units on strategic risk management, collaboration and
        partnerships, and organisational strategy. A response on leadership that only analyses team-level dynamics, when the
        criterion is about organisation-level strategic leadership, has missed the scope of the criterion.
      </p>
      <p>
        Level 7 units that suit senior NHS leaders include Unit 702 (Leading and Developing People to Optimise
        Performance), Unit 708 (Strategic Risk Management), Unit 715 (Strategic Approaches to Equality Diversity and
        Inclusion) and Unit 716 (Strategic Approaches to Mental Health and Wellbeing).
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-7-assignment-help/">CMI Level 7 assignment help</a> works from your unit criteria.
        FCMI membership is a separate matter, based on management experience rather than on completing a Diploma.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="most-common-nhs-units">Units That Suit NHS Managers</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Seven units that fit health and care work across Level 5 and Level 7. No CMI unit is NHS-only; your centre sets which units are in your programme.</p>
      <div class="unit-list">
        <div class="unit-item">
          <div class="unit-number">502</div>
          <div class="unit-body"><h3 class="unit-title">Principles of Developing, Managing and Leading Individuals and Teams to Achieve Success <span class="unit-badge unit-badge--nhs">L5</span></h3>
          <p class="unit-desc">Developing and leading multidisciplinary teams, including under staffing pressure. Note that 502 cannot be combined with 503, 505 or 511.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="unit-item">
          <div class="unit-number">506</div>
          <div class="unit-body"><h3 class="unit-title">Managing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion <span class="unit-badge unit-badge--nhs">L5</span></h3>
          <p class="unit-desc">Published WRES metrics and your trust's equality data can be a strong source of context.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="unit-item">
          <div class="unit-number">514</div>
          <div class="unit-body"><h3 class="unit-title">Managing Change <span class="unit-badge unit-badge--nhs">L5</span></h3>
          <p class="unit-desc">A real service change, such as redesigning a care pathway, gives you a case to analyse. The indicative content names change models such as Kotter, Lewin and ADKAR.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="unit-item">
          <div class="unit-number">507</div>
          <div class="unit-body"><h3 class="unit-title">Principles of Delivering Coaching and Mentoring <span class="unit-badge unit-badge--nhs">L5</span></h3>
          <p class="unit-desc">Coaching and mentoring in supervision and line-management settings.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="unit-item">
          <div class="unit-number">518</div>
          <div class="unit-body"><h3 class="unit-title">Risk Management <span class="unit-badge unit-badge--nhs">L5</span></h3>
          <p class="unit-desc">Risk in a clinical or service setting, where your trust risk register and CQC expectations can supply context.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="unit-item">
          <div class="unit-number">714</div>
          <div class="unit-body"><h3 class="unit-title">Personal and Professional Development for Strategic Leaders <span class="unit-badge unit-badge--nhs">L7</span></h3>
          <p class="unit-desc">A reflective unit built around your own development as a strategic leader, with professional standards and competency frameworks as reference points.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="unit-item">
          <div class="unit-number">715</div>
          <div class="unit-body"><h3 class="unit-title">Strategic Approaches to Equality Diversity and Inclusion <span class="unit-badge unit-badge--nhs">L7</span></h3>
          <p class="unit-desc">Strategic approaches to workforce equality and inclusion at organisational scale, for senior leaders.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="cqc-wres-alignment">Using CQC, WRES and NHS Sources as Evidence</h2>
      <p>
        NHS managers have access to public, NHS-specific sources that can make an assignment specific to their service.
        CMI asks for appropriate use of evidence, examples and references to support conclusions and recommendations,
        so reference anything you use in the style your centre requires.
      </p>
      <div class="ref-grid">
        <div class="ref-block">
          <h3>CQC Well-Led Framework</h3>
          <p>Relevant to leadership and governance units. For Unit 502 at Level 5 or Unit 701 at Level 7, your trust's published CQC inspection outcomes can supply real evidence for the criterion you are answering.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ref-block">
          <h3>WRES Metrics</h3>
          <p>Published annually by NHS England, WRES data is a measurable source for Unit 506 (Managing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ref-block">
          <h3>NHS People Plan</h3>
          <p>The plan and its themes on looking after people and belonging in the NHS can support strategic-scope work in units such as 701 and 715.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ref-block">
          <h3>Integrated Care Systems</h3>
          <p>ICS governance and collaborative leadership give strategic-level context for Units 701 and 703.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        If you use internal trust data rather than published reports, check your employer's confidentiality rules and
        your centre's guidance on anonymising it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="nhs-time-pressure">Studying CMI Alongside an NHS Role — How Assignment Help Works</h2>
      <p>
        Health and care managers often study around demanding schedules: staffing gaps, patient safety concerns,
        inspection readiness and appraisal cycles. Assignment support has to be quick to arrange and written to the
        criteria in your brief.
      </p>
      <p>
        We can write your assignment to your brief, or tutor you through writing it yourself. Either way the work
        follows the verbs and criteria of your unit, set in your own service where your brief allows.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>The process:</strong> send the unit brief, the level, your current status (not started,
        mid-draft, or post-Refer), and the submission deadline via WhatsApp. A fixed quote is provided
        within two hours.
      </p>
      <div class="order-cta">
        <a href={whatsappUrl} class="btn btn-whatsapp btn-lg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Send Your Unit Brief on WhatsApp
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="nhs-cmi-faq">CMI Assignment Help for NHS Managers — Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Which CMI level should an NHS manager study?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><p>CMI does not map its qualifications to NHS pay bands, so choose by the scope of your role. CMI designed Level 5 for managers in roles such as Operations Manager, Departmental Manager and Specialist Manager who lead and manage individuals and teams, typically accountable to a senior manager. It designed Level 7 for practising or aspiring senior managers and leaders in roles such as Senior Manager, Director and CEO. Your centre and employer will confirm the right level for you.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Does the NHS fund CMI qualifications?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><p>Funding depends on your employer. Some trusts and other NHS organisations support management qualifications through their learning and development budgets, but we cannot say what yours offers. Ask your line manager or workforce development team, and check whether a particular level or provider is required.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Which CMI units are specific to NHS and health and social care?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><p>No CMI unit is written only for the NHS, but several suit health and care managers. At Level 5, Unit 506 (Managing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion), Unit 514 (Managing Change) and Unit 518 (Risk Management) are natural choices. At Level 7, Unit 708 (Strategic Risk Management) and Unit 703 (Collaboration and Partnerships) suit governance and Integrated Care System leadership, and Unit 715 (Strategic Approaches to Equality Diversity and Inclusion) and Unit 716 (Strategic Approaches to Mental Health and Wellbeing) suit workforce inclusion and wellbeing strategy. Your centre sets which units are in your programme.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Can I use CQC inspection reports as evidence in my CMI assignment?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><p>Published CQC reports are public documents and can be a useful source of context, with a proper reference. CMI asks for appropriate use of evidence, examples and references to support conclusions. If you use internal trust data, check your employer's confidentiality rules and your centre's guidance on anonymising it.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">I am an NHS manager studying CMI Level 5. Can you help with my unit?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Send your brief, level, and deadline via WhatsApp for a fixed quote within two hours.</p></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Related CMI Assignment Services</h2>
      <div class="supp-grid">
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-5-assignment-help/" class="supp-card"><h3>CMI Level 5 Assignment Help</h3><p>All 26 Level 5 units (501 to 526), written to the unit criteria and command verbs.</p></a>
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-level-7-assignment-help/" class="supp-card"><h3>CMI Level 7 Assignment Help</h3><p>All 16 Group A units (701 to 716), for senior health and care leaders.</p></a>
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-assignment-writing-service/" class="supp-card"><h3>CMI Assignment Writing Service</h3><p>Full assignment support for all NHS levels and units.</p></a>
        <a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-assignment-tutoring/" class="supp-card"><h3>CMI Assignment Tutoring</h3><p>For NHS managers who want to write their own assignment with expert guidance.</p></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title">Related CMI Unit Pages</h2>
      <p>Unit-level support for the units most relevant to this guide:</p>
      <ul class="unit-links">
        <li><a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-506-assignment-help/">CMI Unit 506 assignment help</a>: Managing Equality, Diversity and Inclusion (Level 5)</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-514-assignment-help/">CMI Unit 514 assignment help</a>: Managing Change (Level 5)</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-714-assignment-help/">CMI Unit 714 assignment help</a>: Personal and Professional Development for Strategic Leaders (Level 7)</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-704-assignment-help/">CMI Unit 704 assignment help</a>: Developing Organisational Strategy (Level 7)</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/cmi-715-assignment-help/">CMI Unit 715 assignment help</a>: Strategic Approaches to Equality Diversity and Inclusion (Level 7)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title">Related CMI Guides</h2>
      <p>More guides that connect to this topic:</p>
      <ul class="unit-links">
        <li><a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/cmi-level-5-vs-level-7/">CMI Level 5 vs Level 7</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/is-cmi-qualification-worth-it/">Is a CMI Qualification Worth It?</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/cmi-qualification-levels-explained/">CMI Qualification Levels Explained</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.cmiassignmenthelp.uk.com/guides/cmi-membership-levels-acmi-mcmi-fcmi/">CMI Membership: ACMI, MCMI and FCMI</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="container cta-inner">
      <h2>WhatsApp for a Quote — NHS and Health and Care Managers</h2>
      <p>Send your unit brief and deadline. UK-based CMI writers and tutors, fixed quote within two hours.</p>
      <a href={whatsappUrl} class="btn btn-whatsapp btn-lg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Get NHS CMI Assignment Help
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--navy) 0%, var(--blue) 100%); color: #fff; padding: 5rem 0 4rem; text-align: center; }
  .hero-inner { max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .eyebrow { font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; color: #93c5fd; margin-bottom: .75rem; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.6vw, 2.5rem); font-weight: 800; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.25; }
  .hero-sub { font-size: 1.05rem; color: #bfdbfe; margin-bottom: 2rem; line-height: 1.7; }

  .narrow { max-width: 860px; }

  .band-table { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .75rem; }
  .band-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; }
  .band-row--highlight { border-color: var(--blue); }
  .band-name { background: var(--navy); color: #fff; font-weight: 700; padding: 1.25rem; display: flex; align-items: center; }
  .band-detail { padding: 1.25rem; background: var(--bg-light); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .4rem; font-size: .9rem; }
  .band-roles { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: .82rem; }
  .band-note { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 1rem; font-style: italic; }

  .unit-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
  .unit-item { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3.5rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .unit-item--priority { background: var(--bg-light); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1rem; border-bottom: none; }
  .unit-number { font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--blue); text-align: center; }
  .unit-title { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: .35rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .unit-badge { font-size: .65rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; background: var(--green); color: #fff; padding: .15rem .5rem; border-radius: 20px; }
  .unit-badge--nhs { background: var(--blue); }
  .unit-desc { font-size: .88rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }

  .ref-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .ref-block { background: var(--bg-light); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; }
  .ref-block h3 { font-size: .95rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: .5rem; }
